        "original_id": "4a306e44-38cc-5cf7-aa02-c19f0ee4052f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arturo Ripstein, Bahman Ghobadi, Marga López, Jorge Martínez de Hoyos\n- Places: Mexico, Baneh, Kurdistan province, Iran\n- Works: Tiempo de Morir, Marooned in Iraq\n- Roles: film directors, actors\n\nFacts:\n- Arturo Ripstein y Rosen was born on December 13, 1943 and is a Mexican film director.\n- Bahman Ghobadi was born on February 1, 1969 in Baneh, Kurdistan province.\n- Tiempo de Morir is a 1966 Mexican Western film directed by Arturo Ripstein and starring Marga López and Jorge Martínez de Hoyos.\n- Marooned in Iraq is a 2002 Iranian film in Kurdish and Persian directed by Bahman Ghobadi and produced in Iran.\n- Marooned in Iraq is also known as Songs of My Motherland.",
